        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "该损坏符合Gitaly因unclean shutdown导致ref文件未fsync而损坏的典型模式：refs未被fsync，而git对象本身完好。",
      "certainty": "supported",
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "D-d4521cbf2763ce67e2eb",
          "quote": "For all we know commits and git objects themselves are not lost, but in some cases refs getting updated might result in them getting stored as an empty file.\nIt is likely, that gitaly wants to update the ref, but did not sync the content to disk before having the host fail, so the file containing the ref was corrupted in the process.\n\nObjects are fine (with errors being detectable that is) as they are hashed, and `fsync()`ed by git (<https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/gitaly/-/issues/1727>), but refs are not. Not even when updated via `git update-ref`."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "actions": [
    {
      "text": "执行 `sudo -u git git fsck` 检查 demo/team-alpha 仓库以识别所有 invalid sha1 pointer 错误。",
      "command": "sudo -u git git fsck",
      "prerequisites": "需先定位仓库路径（如 `/var/opt/gitlab/git-data/repositories/@hashed/.../.git`）并 `cd` 进入该目录；所有写入仓库的操作必须以 `sudo -u git` 执行，否则可能破坏文件系统权限。",
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "D-ecede5bebb0136fdc5e2",
          "quote": "## Identifying the damage\n\nAny of these commands writing to the repo must be prefixed with `sudo -u git`, or you might corrupt filesystem permissions!\n\n`git fsck` will provide you with an outline of the damage.\n\n```\nChecking object directories: 100% (256/256), done.\nChecking objects: 100% (1206/1206), done.\nerror: refs/keep-around/0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567: invalid sha1 pointer 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\nerror: refs/merge-requests/42/merge: invalid sha1 pointer 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\nerror: refs/pipelines/123456789: invalid sha1 pointer 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\nerror: refs/tags/v1.1: invalid sha1 pointer 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\nerror: refs/heads/master: invalid sha1 pointer 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000\ndangling commit 76543210fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210\n```"
        },
        {
          "id": "D-ecede5bebb0136fdc5e2",
          "quote": "## Before you start\n\nOnce you found the gitaly shard and location of the project on that shard (`/var/opt/gitlab/git-data/repositories/@hashed/*.git`) **`cd` into that directory**.\n\nMake a backup! Usually (once in the repo) `sudo tar cvf ~<your user>/<issue_id>.tar .` is enough."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "检查 `packed-refs` 文件内容，确认是否存在 `refs/heads/master` 对应的有效SHA1。",
      "command": "",
      "prerequisites": "注意：`packed-refs` 由 `git gc` 在 housekeeping 时生成，可能过期或不存在；若存在，其格式应为 `0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567 refs/heads/master`。",
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "D-ecede5bebb0136fdc5e2",
          "quote": "### Check `packed-refs` first\n\nIn most cases, a quick look in `packed-refs` (if it exists) will yield the commit-hash you seek. It should look something like this:\n\n```\n0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567 refs/heads/master\n0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567 refs/tags/v1.1\n```\n\n**Note**: These refs are captured at the time of a `git gc` as run in housekeeping. So they might not be up to date or not exist at all. Feel free to use this to restore the primary branch to a known good state, and then continue to look for the most recent commit."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "访问 `https://gitlab.com/demo/team-alpha/activity`（需管理员权限）定位最近提交的完整SHA1，用于恢复 master ref。",
      "command": "",
      "prerequisites": "需管理员账户访问；页面中个别提交链接可能无法加载，但URL中包含完整SHA1；恢复时须确保 ref 指向树内有效提交，后续可用 `git log` 验证连通性。",
      "citations": [
        {
          "id": "D-ecede5bebb0136fdc5e2",
          "quote": "### `refs/heads/*`\n\nThese are user-facing branches of the project. In case of the project's primary branch (such as `main` or `master`), this has to be recreated first for GitLab (and various `git` commands) to function properly.\n\nUnfortunately, this is also the type of ref we have the least redundancy for. Your best bet here is to use the project's activity feed (visit `https://gitlab.com/<namespace>/<project>/activity` via your admin account) to get some info here. Individual links to commits on that page might fail to load, so copy their link which will contain the full hash to the commit.\n\nIn the case of the primary branches it is most important to have the ref pointing to *something* that is in the tree, rather than getting the latest commit (which you might only be able to piece together afterwards). Use your best judgement here to point it to a commit that was definitely on the branch you restore. You can validate this afterwards by running a `git log`. It should print no errors and a continous tree of commits."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
